public import TauCeti.LinearAlgebra.RootSystem.SimplyConnectedRootDatum.LieAlgebra.WeightLattice

/-!
# Chevalley data and their group schemes

Chevalley's construction of a split semisimple group scheme over `ℤ` starts from a faithful
finite-dimensional representation of the split Lie algebra over `ℚ` and an admissible lattice in
it: a lattice spanning the representation and stable under Kostant's `ℤ`-form of the enveloping
algebra. The group scheme is the closed subgroup scheme of `GLₙ` generated by the divided-power
exponentials of the root vectors together with a split torus acting on the weight spaces.

For a valid Dynkin type `t`, a **Chevalley datum** `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum t ht`
bundles exactly these inputs for the pinned Lie algebra `TauCeti.DynkinType.lieAlgebra t ht`, read
through the numbered Chevalley generators of `TauCeti.DynkinType.lieBasis`: the representation,
its faithfulness, an admissible lattice for the simple-generator Kostant form, a basis of that
lattice by weight vectors with integral weights `wt j : Fin t.rank → ℤ` (in fundamental-weight
coordinates), and a `ℤ`-basis `b_D` of the **weight lattice** `Λ(D)`, the sublattice of
`Fin t.rank → ℤ` spanned by the weights.

The basis `b_D` is what makes the torus of the group the right one. Writing every weight in
`b_D`-coordinates gives the **coordinate weights**, which span `Fin t.rank → ℤ` by construction
(`TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.span_range_coordinateWeight_eq_top`). The torus they
parametrize is the split torus with character lattice `Λ(D)`, and it is a closed subgroup of the
group scheme (`TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.isClosedImmersion_torus`). Reading the weights
themselves in `Fin t.rank → ℤ` would instead parametrize the torus by the full weight lattice;
when `Λ(D)` is a proper sublattice, that map to `GLₙ` has a nontrivial kernel, the diagonalizable
group with character group `(Fin t.rank → ℤ) / Λ(D)`.

The nilpotence of the root generators, which the divided-power exponentials need, is not part of
the data: a root vector raises weights by a nonzero root, so it acts nilpotently on a space spanned
by finitely many weight vectors
(`TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.isNilpotent_representation_rootGenerator`).

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum`: a Chevalley datum of a valid Dynkin type.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.weightLattice`: the lattice `Λ(D)` spanned by its weights.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.coordinateWeight`: the weights in `b_D`-coordinates.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.coordinateRoot`: the roots in `b_D`-coordinates.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.groupScheme`: its group scheme over `ℤ`, the closed subgroup
  scheme of `GLₙ` generated by the root subgroups of the numbered generators and the torus.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.points`: the points of the group scheme with values in a
  commutative ring, as a subgroup of the general linear group.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.torus`: the split torus with character lattice `Λ(D)`, as a
  morphism into the group scheme.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.torusPoints`: the same torus on points with values in a
  commutative ring.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.span_range_coordinateWeight_eq_top`: the coordinate weights
  span `Fin t.rank → ℤ`.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.root_mem_weightLattice`: every root lies in `Λ(D)`.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.isNilpotent_representation_rootGenerator`: the numbered root
  generators act nilpotently.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.isClosedImmersion_torus`: the torus is a closed subgroup of
  the group scheme.

## References

* R. Steinberg, *Lectures on Chevalley Groups*, AMS University Lecture Series 66 (2016),
  Chapters 2 and 3.
* J. E. Humphreys, *Linear Algebraic Groups*, §27.
* J. C. Jantzen, *Representations of Algebraic Groups*, II.1.
-/

public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory

namespace TauCeti.DynkinType

universe v

/-- A **Chevalley datum** of a valid Dynkin type `t`: a faithful representation of the pinned Lie
algebra `TauCeti.DynkinType.lieAlgebra t ht` over `ℚ`, a lattice in it that spans it and is stable
under the simple-generator Kostant form, a basis of that lattice by weight vectors with integral
weights in fundamental-weight coordinates, and a `ℤ`-basis of the lattice spanned by those
weights. These are the inputs of Chevalley's construction of a split group scheme over `ℤ`. -/
structure ChevalleyDatum (t : DynkinType) (ht : t.Valid) where
  /-- The rational representation space. -/
  carrier : Type
  [instAddCommGroup : AddCommGroup carrier]
  [instModule : Module ℚ carrier]
  /-- The representation of the pinned Lie algebra, extended to its enveloping algebra. -/
  representation :
    _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra ℚ (t.lieAlgebra ht) →ₐ[ℚ] Module.End ℚ carrier
  /-- The representation is faithful on the Lie algebra. -/
  injective_representation_ι :
    Function.Injective fun x : t.lieAlgebra ht =>
      representation (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι ℚ x)
  /-- The admissible lattice. -/
  lattice : AddSubgroup carrier
  /-- The lattice is stable under the simple-generator Kostant form. -/
  representation_mem_lattice :
    ∀ u ∈ UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantForm (t.lieBasis ht).rootGenerator (t.lieBasis ht).h,
      ∀ m ∈ lattice, representation u m ∈ lattice
  /-- The lattice spans the representation space over `ℚ`. -/
  span_lattice_eq_top : Submodule.span ℚ (lattice : Set carrier) = ⊤
  /-- The rank of the lattice. -/
  dim : ℕ
  /-- The weight basis of the lattice. -/
  basis : Module.Basis (Fin dim) ℤ lattice
  /-- The integral weight of each basis vector, in fundamental-weight coordinates. -/
  weight : Fin dim → Fin t.rank → ℤ
  /-- Each basis vector is a weight vector of its recorded weight. -/
  isCartanWeightVector_basis (j : Fin dim) :
    UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.IsCartanWeightVector (t.lieBasis ht).h representation (weight j)
      (basis j : carrier)
  /-- A `ℤ`-basis of the lattice spanned by the weights. -/
  weightLatticeBasis : Module.Basis (Fin t.rank) ℤ (Submodule.span ℤ (Set.range weight))

namespace ChevalleyDatum

variable {t : DynkinType} {ht : t.Valid} (D : ChevalleyDatum t ht)

attribute [instance] instAddCommGroup instModule

instance : CoeSort (ChevalleyDatum t ht) Type := ⟨carrier⟩

/-! ## The weight lattice and the coordinate weights -/

/-- The **weight lattice** `Λ(D)` of a Chevalley datum: the sublattice of `Fin t.rank → ℤ` spanned
by the weights of its weight basis.

This is an abbreviation so that the chosen basis `D.weightLatticeBasis` is a basis of
`D.weightLattice` without transport. -/
abbrev weightLattice : Submodule ℤ (Fin t.rank → ℤ) :=
  Submodule.span ℤ (Set.range D.weight)

/-- The weight lattice is the integral span of the weights. -/
theorem weightLattice_def : D.weightLattice = Submodule.span ℤ (Set.range D.weight) :=
  (rfl)

/-- Each weight of the weight basis lies in the weight lattice. -/
theorem weight_mem_weightLattice (j : Fin D.dim) : D.weight j ∈ D.weightLattice :=
  Submodule.subset_span ⟨j, rfl⟩

/-- The **coordinate weight** of a basis vector: its weight, written in the chosen basis of the
weight lattice. These are the characters through which the torus with character lattice `Λ(D)`
acts on the weight basis. -/
noncomputable def coordinateWeight (j : Fin D.dim) : Fin t.rank → ℤ :=
  D.weightLatticeBasis.repr ⟨D.weight j, D.weight_mem_weightLattice j⟩

/-- **The coordinate weights are the coordinates of the weights**: recombining the chosen basis of
the weight lattice with them recovers the weights. -/
theorem sum_coordinateWeight_smul (j : Fin D.dim) :
    ∑ i, D.coordinateWeight j i • (D.weightLatticeBasis i : Fin t.rank → ℤ) = D.weight j := by
  have h := congrArg Subtype.val
    (D.weightLatticeBasis.sum_repr ⟨D.weight j, D.weight_mem_weightLattice j⟩)
  rwa [Submodule.coe_sum] at h

/-- The coordinate weight of a basis vector is the coordinate vector of its weight in the chosen
basis of the weight lattice. -/
theorem coordinateWeight_def (j : Fin D.dim) :
    D.coordinateWeight j = D.weightLatticeBasis.repr ⟨D.weight j, D.weight_mem_weightLattice j⟩ :=
  (rfl)

/-- **The coordinate weights span the character lattice.** The weights span `Λ(D)` by definition,
and reading `Λ(D)` in the chosen basis is a linear isomorphism onto `Fin t.rank → ℤ`. -/
theorem span_range_coordinateWeight_eq_top :
    Submodule.span ℤ (Set.range D.coordinateWeight) = ⊤ := by
  have hrange : Set.range D.coordinateWeight =
      D.weightLatticeBasis.equivFun '' ((↑) ⁻¹' Set.range D.weight) := by
    ext μ
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨j, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨⟨D.weight j, D.weight_mem_weightLattice j⟩, ⟨j, rfl⟩,
        D.weightLatticeBasis.equivFun_apply _⟩
    · rintro ⟨⟨_, _⟩, ⟨j, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨j, (D.weightLatticeBasis.equivFun_apply _).symm⟩
  rw [hrange, Submodule.span_image_linearEquiv, Submodule.span_span_coe_preimage,
    Submodule.map_top, LinearEquiv.range]

/-! ## The roots in the weight lattice -/

/-- **Every root lies in the weight lattice.** A faithful representation sees every simple root as
a difference of two of its weights, and the simple roots span the root lattice. -/
theorem root_mem_weightLattice (γ : Fin t.numRoots) :
    (t.simplyConnectedRootDatum ht).root γ ∈ D.weightLattice :=
  rootSpan_le_span_weight ht D.representation D.lattice D.representation_mem_lattice D.basis
    D.weight D.injective_representation_ι D.span_lattice_eq_top D.isCartanWeightVector_basis
    (Submodule.subset_span ⟨γ, rfl⟩)

/-- The **coordinate root** of a root `γ`: the root, written in the chosen basis of the weight
lattice. It is the character of the torus with character lattice `Λ(D)` through which that torus
acts on the root subgroup of `γ`. -/
noncomputable def coordinateRoot (γ : Fin t.numRoots) : Fin t.rank → ℤ :=
  D.weightLatticeBasis.repr ⟨_, D.root_mem_weightLattice γ⟩

/-- The coordinate root is the coordinate vector of the root in the chosen basis of the weight
lattice. -/
theorem coordinateRoot_def (γ : Fin t.numRoots) :
    D.coordinateRoot γ = D.weightLatticeBasis.repr ⟨_, D.root_mem_weightLattice γ⟩ :=
  (rfl)

/-- **The coordinate roots are the coordinates of the roots**: recombining the chosen basis of the
weight lattice with them recovers the roots. -/
theorem sum_coordinateRoot_smul (γ : Fin t.numRoots) :
    ∑ i, D.coordinateRoot γ i • (D.weightLatticeBasis i : Fin t.rank → ℤ) =
      (t.simplyConnectedRootDatum ht).root γ := by
  have h := congrArg Subtype.val (D.weightLatticeBasis.sum_repr ⟨_, D.root_mem_weightLattice γ⟩)
  rwa [Submodule.coe_sum] at h

/-! ## Nilpotence of the root generators -/

/-- **The lattice spans the representation space through its weight basis.** -/
theorem span_range_basis_eq_top :
    Submodule.span ℚ (Set.range fun j => (D.basis j : D.carrier)) = ⊤ := by
  have h := D.basis.span_range_eq_span_range_basis (S := ℚ) D.lattice.subtype.toIntLinearMap
  rw [AddMonoidHom.coe_toIntLinearMap, AddSubgroup.coe_subtype, Subtype.range_coe,
    D.span_lattice_eq_top] at h
  exact h.symm

/-- **The numbered root generators act nilpotently.** Each of them raises weights by a nonzero
root, and the representation is spanned by finitely many weight vectors. -/
theorem isNilpotent_representation_rootGenerator (i : Fin t.rank ⊕ Fin t.rank) :
    IsNilpotent (D.representation
      (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι ℚ ((t.lieBasis ht).rootGenerator i))) :=
  UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.isNilpotent_of_isCartanWeightVector (t.lieBasis ht).h
    D.representation D.isCartanWeightVector_basis D.span_range_basis_eq_top
    (t.lie_lieBasis_h_rootGenerator ht i) (t.rootGeneratorWeight_ne_zero ht i)

/-! ## The group scheme -/

/-- **The group scheme of a Chevalley datum**: the smallest closed subgroup scheme of `GLₙ` over
`ℤ`, for `n` the rank of the lattice, containing the divided-power exponential root subgroups of
the numbered Chevalley generators and the split torus acting on the weight basis through the
coordinate weights.

This is an abbreviation, like the Kostant toral closure it specializes, so that the inclusion into
`GLₙ`, the torus and the points of that construction apply to it without transport. -/
noncomputable abbrev groupScheme : Grp (Over (Spec (CommRingCat.of ℤ))) :=
  UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantToralGroupScheme (t.lieBasis ht).rootGenerator
    (t.lieBasis ht).h D.representation D.lattice D.representation_mem_lattice
    D.isNilpotent_representation_rootGenerator D.basis D.coordinateWeight

/-- The closed immersion of the group scheme of a Chevalley datum into `GLₙ`. -/
noncomputable def groupSchemeι : D.groupScheme ⟶ GeneralLinear.groupScheme ℤ D.dim :=
  UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantToralGroupSchemeι (t.lieBasis ht).rootGenerator
    (t.lieBasis ht).h D.representation D.lattice D.representation_mem_lattice
    D.isNilpotent_representation_rootGenerator D.basis D.coordinateWeight

/-- The inclusion of the group scheme of a Chevalley datum is the inclusion of its Kostant toral
closure. -/
theorem groupSchemeι_def :
    D.groupSchemeι =
      UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantToralGroupSchemeι (t.lieBasis ht).rootGenerator
        (t.lieBasis ht).h D.representation D.lattice D.representation_mem_lattice
        D.isNilpotent_representation_rootGenerator D.basis D.coordinateWeight :=
  (rfl)

/-- The group scheme of a Chevalley datum is a closed subgroup scheme of `GLₙ`. -/
instance isClosedImmersion_groupSchemeι : IsClosedImmersion D.groupSchemeι.hom.hom.left :=
  UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.isClosedImmersion_kostantToralGroupSchemeι _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _

/-- **The points of a Chevalley datum** with values in a commutative ring `A`: the subgroup of
`GLₙ(A)` cut out by the defining Hopf ideal of its group scheme. -/
noncomputable def points (A : Type v) [CommRing A] :
    Subgroup (Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup (Fin D.dim) A) :=
  UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantToralPointsSubgroup (t.lieBasis ht).rootGenerator
    (t.lieBasis ht).h D.representation D.lattice D.representation_mem_lattice
    D.isNilpotent_representation_rootGenerator D.basis D.coordinateWeight A

/-- The points of a Chevalley datum are the points of the Kostant toral closure it specializes,
so the generic API of those points applies to them. -/
theorem points_eq_kostantToralPointsSubgroup (A : Type v) [CommRing A] :
    D.points A =
      UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantToralPointsSubgroup (t.lieBasis ht).rootGenerator
        (t.lieBasis ht).h D.representation D.lattice D.representation_mem_lattice
        D.isNilpotent_representation_rootGenerator D.basis D.coordinateWeight A :=
  (rfl)

/-- The points of a Chevalley datum are the invertible matrices cut out by the defining Hopf ideal
of its group scheme. -/
theorem points_def (A : Type v) [CommRing A] :
    D.points A =
      GeneralLinear.hopfIdealPointsSubgroup D.dim
        (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantToralDefiningIdeal (t.lieBasis ht).rootGenerator
          (t.lieBasis ht).h D.representation D.lattice D.representation_mem_lattice
          D.isNilpotent_representation_rootGenerator D.basis D.coordinateWeight) A :=
  UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantToralPointsSubgroup_def _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ A

/-- Membership in the points of a Chevalley datum is vanishing on the defining Hopf ideal of its
group scheme. -/
@[simp]
theorem mem_points_iff (A : Type v) [CommRing A] (g : Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup (Fin D.dim) A) :
    g ∈ D.points A ↔
      ∀ x ∈ UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantToralDefiningIdeal (t.lieBasis ht).rootGenerator
          (t.lieBasis ht).h D.representation D.lattice D.representation_mem_lattice
          D.isNilpotent_representation_rootGenerator D.basis D.coordinateWeight,
        ((GeneralLinear.pointsMulEquiv (R := ℤ) D.dim).symm g).ofConv x = 0 :=
  UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.mem_kostantToralPointsSubgroup_iff _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ A g

/-- Every matrix in a numbered root subgroup of a Chevalley datum is a point of it. -/
theorem kostantRootSubgroupMatrix_mem_points (A : Type v) [CommRing A]
    (i : Fin t.rank ⊕ Fin t.rank)
    (q : HopfAlgebra.points (R := ℤ) (H := AdditiveGroup.coordinateHopfAlgebra ℤ)
      (CommAlgCat.of ℤ A)) :
    UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantRootSubgroupMatrix (t.lieBasis ht).rootGenerator
        (t.lieBasis ht).h D.representation D.lattice D.representation_mem_lattice i
        (D.isNilpotent_representation_rootGenerator i) D.basis q ∈ D.points A :=
  UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantGeneratedPointsSubgroup_le_toralPoints _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ A
    (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantRootSubgroupMatrix_mem_generatedPoints
      _ _ _ _ _ _ _ A i q)

/-- Every matrix of the torus of a Chevalley datum, acting on each weight basis vector through its
coordinate weight, is a point of it. -/
theorem kostantTorusMatrix_mem_points (A : Type v) [CommRing A] (s : Fin t.rank → Aˣ) :
    UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantTorusMatrix D.lattice D.basis D.coordinateWeight s ∈
      D.points A :=
  UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantTorusMatrix_mem_toralPoints _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ A s

/-! ## The torus -/

/-- **The torus of a Chevalley datum**: the split torus over `ℤ` with character lattice `Λ(D)`,
identified with `Fin t.rank → ℤ` by the chosen basis, acting on each weight basis vector through
its coordinate weight. -/
noncomputable def torus : SplitTorus.groupScheme ℤ (Fin t.rank) ⟶ D.groupScheme :=
  UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantWeightTorusToToral (t.lieBasis ht).rootGenerator
    (t.lieBasis ht).h D.representation D.lattice D.representation_mem_lattice
    D.isNilpotent_representation_rootGenerator D.basis D.coordinateWeight

/-- Included into `GLₙ`, the torus of a Chevalley datum is the weight torus of its coordinate
weights. -/
@[simp]
theorem torus_comp_groupSchemeι :
    D.torus ≫ D.groupSchemeι = GeneralLinear.weightTorus (R := ℤ) D.coordinateWeight :=
  UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantWeightTorusToToral_comp_ι _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _

/-- **The torus of a Chevalley datum on points** with values in a commutative ring `A`: the point
`s : Fin t.rank → Aˣ` of the split torus, read in the chosen basis of `Λ(D)`, acts on each weight
basis vector by the value at `s` of its coordinate weight. -/
noncomputable def torusPoints (A : Type v) [CommRing A] : (Fin t.rank → Aˣ) →* D.points A :=
  MonoidHom.codRestrict
    (UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantTorusMatrix D.lattice D.basis D.coordinateWeight)
    (D.points A) (D.kostantTorusMatrix_mem_points A)

/-- A torus point of a Chevalley datum is the diagonal matrix of the values of the coordinate
weights. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_torusPoints (A : Type v) [CommRing A] (s : Fin t.rank → Aˣ) :
    (D.torusPoints A s : Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup (Fin D.dim) A) =
      UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantTorusMatrix D.lattice D.basis D.coordinateWeight s :=
  (rfl)

/-- **The torus of a Chevalley datum is a closed subgroup of its group scheme**, because its
coordinate weights span the character lattice. -/
instance isClosedImmersion_torus : IsClosedImmersion D.torus.hom.hom.left :=
  UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.isClosedImmersion_kostantWeightTorusToToral _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _
    D.span_range_coordinateWeight_eq_top

end ChevalleyDatum

end TauCeti.DynkinType
